        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add note for Firefox and Chrome regarding the ability to access local host for development add-ons as per_<a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1864284\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1864284</a> Allow localhost in MV3 CSP to allow connecting to local dev servers_ with the addition of:</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">RelRelated content changes in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3731489249\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42410\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42410/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42410\">mdn/content#42410</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28683",
            "title": "Bug-1864284-Allow-localhost-access-for-temporary-MV3-add-on",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-16T23:04:33.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-16T23:03:31.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">While using the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Storage_Access_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Storage Access API</a>, when embedded content activates a previously-granted <code class=\"notranslate\">storage-access</code> permission via the <code class=\"notranslate\">requestStorageAccess()</code> method or the <code class=\"notranslate\">Activate-Storage-Access</code> header, 3rd party cookies are now only sent with requests to the calling embed's exact origin.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Previously, 3rd party cookies were sent with requests to the calling embed's site.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This behavioral change has occurred in:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Chrome 141: See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5169937372676096\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5169937372676096</a>.</li>\n<li>Firefox 140: See <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/storage-access-api/requestStorageAccess-cross-origin-fetch.sub.https.window.html?run_id=5176618970775552\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/storage-access-api/requestStorageAccess-cross-origin-fetch.sub.https.window.html?run_id=5176618970775552</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds notes in relevant places to document this change.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">cc <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/cfredric/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/cfredric\">@cfredric</a> / <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/hamishwillee/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/hamishwillee\">@hamishwillee</a> — I'd appreciate your input on this one, folks.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28682",
            "title": "Chrome 141/Firefox 140 storage access activation per origin",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-16T23:13:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-16T16:59:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93594?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;div hidden=\"until-found\"&gt;</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;details&gt;</code> auto-open when things are found within them. This landed later than <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;details&gt;</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However, the implementation in Firefox and Safari is buggy.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It feels like the warrants \"partial_implementation\", because it results in the user often not seeing the content they're searching for.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28672",
            "title": "Add details for auto-open-on-find",
